  "Number": 8,
  "Question": "The sums of three whole numbers taken in pairs are \\(12,\\) \\(17,\\) and \\(19.\\) What is the middle number?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(4\\)",
    "B": "\\(5\\)",
    "C": "\\(6\\)",
    "D": "\\(7\\)",
    "E": "\\(8\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Adding all three pair sums is useful because each of the three original numbers appears in exactly two pairs. Thus their sum is\n\\[\n\\frac{12+17+19}{2}=24.\n\\]\nEach pair leaves out one number, so subtracting the three pair sums from \\(24\\) recovers all three numbers:\n\\[\n24-12=12,\\qquad 24-17=7,\\qquad 24-19=5.\n\\]\nIn increasing order they are \\(5,7,12\\). The middle number is \\(\\boxed{7}\\), choice D.",
